      ],
      "scope_limits": [
        "Machine context is available; this does not establish DOS source-address mapping, legacy reply schema, guest process lifecycle or drop-in parity.",
        "Raw MachineContext.run is host-time bounded and returns machine stops. The COM/MZ process session separately verifies parent return for guest_exit/guest_tsr; neither path supplies guest_ms/fast_forward/stop_on_hook semantics.",
        "Raw native QEMU exposes one machine context. dosbox-qemu exposes a DOS CPU plus its surrounding Linux machine; those are different CPUs and cannot be renamed into one native DOS context.",
        "The legacy public DOS route intentionally refuses direct writes (use RAM layers, runtime bindings or edited checkpoints); machine context already permits explicit guarded edits. Preserve legacy refusal and expose new context semantics explicitly.",
        "qemu-machine has its own explicit bounded script grammar and operation set. The full legacy DOS script vocabulary is not supported merely because script() exists."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dos-process",
      "order": 1,
      "title": "Actual DOS boot, source-bound programs and resident drivers",
      "depends_on": [
        "core"
      ],
      "gate": "Boot a real DOS image; admit supplied COM/MZ bytes; observe relocation/PSP/entry, child/parent termination and TSR distinction; pin guest profile and observed task/page mappings.",
      "status": "in_progress",
      "witness_tests": [
        "tests/test_debug_semantics.py",
        "tests/test_debugger.py",
        "tests/test_desqview_memory_native.py",
        "tests/test_desqview_runtime.py",
        "tests/test_dos_launch.py",
        "tests/test_dos_memory.py",
        "tests/test_dos_qemu.py",
        "tests/test_memory_rules.py",
        "tests/test_memory_search_runtime.py",
        "tests/test_protected_runtime_native.py",
        "tests/test_qemu_dos_native.py",
        "tests/test_qemm_runtime.py",
        "tests/test_qemu_machine.py",
        "tests/test_dos_process_helper.py",
        "tests/test_dos_process_image.py",
        "tests/test_qemu_dos_process.py",
        "tests/test_qemu_dos_process_native.py",
        "tests/test_qemu_dos_process_lifecycle.py"
      ],
      "scope_limits": [
        "Original COM/MZ projects launch through real DOS EXEC with a separate private boot disk. Observed PSP/MCB, ordered MZ relocations, exact loader stack writes and native entry establish the initial source map; controls retain machine addresses.",
        "Nonce-bound parent return and DOS AH=4Dh distinguish selected process exit/residency. Resident mappings intersect observed retained allocations; machine close and uncertain observations invalidate live ownership and capture epochs.",
        "Entry requires observed real mode. Patched versions, secondary executable stubs, DPMI/V86 process mapping and real QEMM/DESQview scheduler/driver combinations remain unqualified.",
        "Device-header registration and an authored SYS initialization marker qualify only those observations, not arbitrary device I/O. Game assets/drivers must already be present in the image; existing startup/configuration bytes are preserved."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trace-events",
      "order": 2,
      "title": "Observed execution traces and event searches",
      "depends_on": [
        "core",
        "dos-process"
      ],
      "gate": "Compare explicit trace semantics, instruction/context/mode identity, callback-safe boundaries, new-page/new-region/register predicates, IRQ/fault/REP cases, and action causality.",
      "status": "pending",
      "witness_tests": [
        "tests/test_debug_semantics.py",
        "tests/test_execution_event_native.py",
        "tests/test_execution_trace.py",
        "tests/test_protected_mode_trace.py",
        "tests/test_qemu_machine.py"
      ],
      "scope_limits": [
        "QEMU records completed single steps with IRQ/timer stepping limits; DOSBox records before-fetch boundaries. Do not identify those schemas or silently omit callbacks, faults or unfinished instructions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clock-media-input",
      "order": 3,
